---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const title = "How to Read a Stock Chart — A Visual Guide | SG Market Academy"
const description = "A free visual guide to reading stock charts for beginners. Learn candlesticks, volume, and basic indicators. Join our Singapore learning community on WhatsApp."
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
      :root {
        --page-bg: #f6f5f0;
        --ink: #191919;
        --ink-mid: #555;
        --ink-light: #888;
        --paper: #fffef9;
        --rule: #d4d0c8;
        --accent-red: #c0392b;
        --accent-green: #27ae60;
        --accent-blue: #2980b9;
        --highlight: #fef9c3;
        --font-serif: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif;
        --font-sans: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
        --font-mono: 'Geist Mono', 'SF Mono', monospace;
        --col-max: 42rem;
      }

      body {
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
        background: var(--page-bg);
        color: var(--ink);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      /* --- Layout --- */
      .col {
        max-width: var(--col-max);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
      }
      .col-wide {
        max-width: 56rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
      }

      /* --- Typography --- */
      .serif { font-family: var(--font-serif); }
      .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em; }

      /* --- Lesson elements --- */
      .lesson-step {
        background: var(--paper);
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 2rem 2rem 1.75rem;
        position: relative;
      }
      .lesson-step::before {
        content: attr(data-step);
        position: absolute;
        top: -0.75rem;
        left: 1.5rem;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--paper);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 3px;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      }

      .candle-diagram {
        display: flex;
        align-items: end;
        gap: 0.6rem;
        padding: 1.5rem 0;
        justify-content: center;
      }
      .candle {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0;
      }
      .candle-wick {
        width: 2px;
        background: var(--ink);
      }
      .candle-body {
        width: 1.5rem;
        border-radius: 2px;
        min-height: 1rem;
      }
      .candle-label {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.6rem;
        color: var(--ink-light);
        margin-top: 0.4rem;
      }

      .annotation {
        background: var(--highlight);
        padding: 0.15rem 0.3rem;
        border-radius: 2px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .aside-box {
        border-left: 3px solid var(--rule);
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--ink-mid);
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
      }
      .aside-box.warning {
        border-left-color: var(--accent-red);
        background: #fef2f2;
      }

      .volume-bar {
        border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0;
        min-width: 1.5rem;
      }

      /* CTA */
      .cta-btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        background: #25D366;
        color: white;
        font-weight: 700;
        padding: 0.85rem 1.75rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        transition: background 0.15s ease;
      }
      .cta-btn:hover {
        background: #1a9e4a;
      }

      /* Separator */
      .sep {
        border: none;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        margin: 0;
      }

      /* Quiz */
      .quiz-option {
        background: var(--paper);
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: border-color 0.15s;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      .quiz-option:hover {
        border-color: var(--ink);
      }
      .quiz-option.correct {
        border-color: var(--accent-green);
        background: #f0fdf4;
      }
      .quiz-option.wrong {
        border-color: var(--accent-red);
        background: #fef2f2;
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .lesson-step { padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
      }
    </style>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Article Header -->
  <section style="padding: clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem) 0 2rem;">
    <div class="col text-center">
      <p class="mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-3" style="color: var(--ink-light);">Lesson 01 &mdash; Beginner Guide</p>
      <h1 class="serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl leading-[1.1] mb-5" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        How to Read<br>a Stock Chart
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base max-w-md mx-auto" style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
        A visual walkthrough of the three things every chart shows you — and the one thing no chart can tell you.
      </p>

      <div class="aside-box warning max-w-md mx-auto mt-6 text-left">
        <strong>Not financial advice.</strong> This is educational content explaining how charts work. It does not tell you what to buy or sell. All investing carries risk of loss.
      </div>

      <div class="text-center mt-6">
        <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="link-btn cta-btn" onclick="onLinkBtnClick()">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z"/></svg>
          Join Free WhatsApp Group
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="sep">

  <!-- Step 1: Candlesticks -->
  <section style="padding: clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem) 0;">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lesson-step" data-step="STEP 1">
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4" style="letter-spacing: -0.01em;">The Candlestick: A Story in Four Numbers</h2>

        <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          Each "candle" on a stock chart represents one time period (a day, an hour, etc.) and tells you four things: where the price <span class="annotation">opened</span>, where it <span class="annotation">closed</span>, the <span class="annotation">highest</span> point, and the <span class="annotation">lowest</span> point.
        </p>

        <!-- Visual: annotated candlestick -->
        <div style="background: var(--page-bg); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
          <div style="max-width: 16rem; margin: 0 auto; position: relative;">
            <!-- Green candle anatomy -->
            <svg viewBox="0 0 200 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
              <!-- Wick -->
              <line x1="100" y1="20" x2="100" y2="80" stroke="#191919" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <line x1="100" y1="180" x2="100" y2="240" stroke="#191919" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <!-- Body -->
              <rect x="72" y="80" width="56" height="100" rx="3" fill="#27ae60" stroke="#191919" stroke-width="2"/>
              <!-- Labels -->
              <text x="20" y="24" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="#888">High</text>
              <line x1="55" y1="20" x2="97" y2="20" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
              <text x="20" y="84" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="#27ae60" font-weight="600">Close</text>
              <line x1="55" y1="80" x2="72" y2="80" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
              <text x="135" y="184" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="#27ae60" font-weight="600">Open</text>
              <line x1="128" y1="180" x2="133" y2="180" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
              <text x="135" y="244" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="#888">Low</text>
              <line x1="100" y1="240" x2="133" y2="240" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
              <!-- Arrow label -->
              <text x="56" y="140" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="9" fill="#fff" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 56 140)">BODY</text>
              <text x="110" y="50" font-family="Geist Mono, monospace" font-size="9" fill="#888" transform="rotate(-90 110 50)">WICK</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-center mono text-xs mt-2" style="color: var(--ink-light);">
            Green (bullish): price closed higher than it opened
          </p>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          If the closing price is <strong>higher</strong> than the opening price, the candle is typically <span style="color: var(--accent-green); font-weight: 600;">green</span>. If it closed <strong>lower</strong>, it's <span style="color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 600;">red</span>. That's it. The thin lines (wicks) show the range. The thick part (body) shows open-to-close.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step 2: Reading a series -->
  <section style="padding: 0 0 clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem);">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lesson-step" data-step="STEP 2">
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Multiple Candles = A Narrative</h2>

        <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          One candle tells you what happened in a single period. A <em>series</em> of candles shows a trend over time. Here's what a simple 7-day chart might look like:
        </p>

        <!-- Visual: 7-candle series -->
        <div style="background: var(--page-bg); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
          <div class="candle-diagram">
            <!-- Day 1: small green -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 8px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 18px; background: var(--accent-green);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 5px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Mon</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 2: tall green -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 4px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 32px; background: var(--accent-green);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 6px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Tue</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 3: small green -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 10px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 12px; background: var(--accent-green);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 14px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Wed</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 4: red -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 6px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 24px; background: var(--accent-red);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 10px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Thu</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 5: tall red -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 4px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 36px; background: var(--accent-red);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 3px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Fri</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 6: small red, doji-like -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 16px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 4px; background: var(--accent-red);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 18px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Mon</div>
            </div>
            <!-- Day 7: green recovery -->
            <div class="candle">
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 5px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-body" style="height: 22px; background: var(--accent-green);"></div>
              <div class="candle-wick" style="height: 8px;"></div>
              <div class="candle-label">Tue</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-center mono text-xs" style="color: var(--ink-light);">
            Illustrative only &mdash; not a real stock
          </p>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          You can see an uptrend early in the week, followed by selling pressure on Thursday and Friday. Monday shows indecision (a "doji" — very small body with long wicks), then a green candle on Tuesday. This is just <em>description</em>, not prediction. What happens next is unknown.
        </p>

        <div class="aside-box">
          <strong>Key concept:</strong> Charts show what <em>has happened</em>. They cannot tell you what <em>will happen</em>. This is the single most important thing to remember.
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-4">
          <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="link-btn cta-btn" onclick="onLinkBtnClick()">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z"/></svg>
            Discuss Charts with Peers
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step 3: Volume -->
  <section style="padding: 0 0 clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem);">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lesson-step" data-step="STEP 3">
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Volume: How Many People Participated</h2>

        <p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          Below most charts you'll see a bar chart — that's <span class="annotation">volume</span>. It tells you how many shares were traded during that period. Higher volume means more market participants were active.
        </p>

        <!-- Visual: volume bars -->
        <div style="background: var(--page-bg); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6rem; height: 80px;">
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 30%; background: var(--accent-green); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 65%; background: var(--accent-green); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 40%; background: var(--accent-green); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 55%; background: var(--accent-red); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 90%; background: var(--accent-red); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 25%; background: var(--accent-red); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
            <div class="volume-bar" style="height: 45%; background: var(--accent-green); width: 1.5rem;"></div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">M</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">T</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">W</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">T</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px] font-bold" style="color: var(--accent-red); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">F</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">M</span>
            <span class="mono text-[10px]" style="color: var(--ink-light); width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">T</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-center mono text-xs mt-3" style="color: var(--ink-light);">
            Notice Friday's spike &mdash; more participants during the big red candle
          </p>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          Volume alone doesn't tell you direction. A high-volume day could mean heavy buying <em>or</em> heavy selling. It simply means: a lot of people traded. It adds context to price movement, nothing more.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step 4: What charts CAN'T do -->
  <section style="padding: 0 0 clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem);">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lesson-step" data-step="STEP 4">
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">What Charts Cannot Tell You</h2>

        <p class="mb-5" style="color: var(--ink-mid);">
          This is the most important part of the lesson. Charts are a record of what happened. They are not:
        </p>

        <div style="display: grid; gap: 0.75rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: start; gap: 0.75rem; background: #fef2f2; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-red);">
            <span style="color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">&times;</span>
            <span class="text-sm" style="color: var(--ink-mid);"><strong>Not a crystal ball.</strong> Past patterns do not predict future prices. Markets can do anything at any time.</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: start; gap: 0.75rem; background: #fef2f2; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-red);">
            <span style="color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">&times;</span>
            <span class="text-sm" style="color: var(--ink-mid);"><strong>Not a buy/sell signal.</strong> No chart formation obligates the market to move in any direction.</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: start; gap: 0.75rem; background: #fef2f2; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-red);">
            <span style="color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">&times;</span>
            <span class="text-sm" style="color: var(--ink-mid);"><strong>Not a guarantee of anything.</strong> All investing involves risk. You can lose some or all of your capital.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="aside-box mt-5">
          Chart reading is a <em>literacy skill</em>, like reading a financial statement. Being able to read a chart does not mean you should trade. It means you understand what you're looking at.
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-4">
          <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="link-btn cta-btn" onclick="onLinkBtnClick()">
